    source: "exam01",
    sourceLabel: "Exam 01 practice key",
    text: "[Exam 01 practice key · converged? · Q2] What is a \"hidden state\" in an RNN? What information does it carry? The hidden state is a vector that serves as the RNN's \"memory.\" At each time step, it is updated based on the current input and the previous hidden state. It carries a compressed summary of all the information the network has seen so far in the sequence. It's the mechanism that allows the RNN to use context from earlier tokens when processing later tokens.",
