    text: "[Exam 01 practice key · (SGD)\"? · Q4] Explain why the hidden state becomes a problem for long sequences. The hidden state is a fixed-size vector that must compress all information from the entire sequence so far. As the sequence gets longer, earlier information gets increasingly diluted as new information is added. If token at position 5 is critical for predicting position 500, that information has been processed through ~495 updates, each potentially overwriting or degrading it. The fixed-size hidden state creates a \"bottleneck\" that loses information over long distances.",
