    text: "[Exam 01 practice key · In self-attention, every token's query is compared to every token's key in a single matrix · Q4] What is the difference between \"training loss\" and \"validation loss\"? Why do we track both? Training loss measures how well the model fits the data it's actively learning from. Validation loss measures how well the model performs on unseen data it has never trained on. We track both to detect overfitting: if training loss keeps decreasing but validation loss starts increasing, the model is memorizing the training data rather than learning generalizable patterns.",
