    source: "exam02",
    sourceLabel: "Practice packet 02 key",
    text: "[Practice packet 02 key · Post-Training Overview · Q1] What is “post-training” and how does it differ from pre-training? Be specific about the data, the loss function, and what the model is learning. Post-training is any training applied to a model after the initial large-scale self-supervised pre-training phase. Pre-training uses huge unlabeled text corpora and a plain next-token cross-entropy loss to learn general language modeling. Post-training uses much smaller, curated datasets (instruction pairs, preferences, demonstrations) and is aimed at teaching the model specific behaviors -- being helpful, following instructions, refusing harmful requests, etc. The loss functions vary: SFT still uses cross-entropy, but only on the response; RLHF uses a reinforcement-learning objective with a reward model; DPO uses a preference-based classification loss.",
