    sourceLabel: "Practice packet 02 key",
    text: "[Practice packet 02 key · describe · Q9] DPO (Direct Preference Optimization) gets rid of the reward model entirely. Describe the core idea in 2-3 sentences. DPO reparameterizes the RLHF objective so you can train directly on (prompt, chosen, rejected) preference triples with a simple classification-style loss -- no separate reward model and no PPO loop needed. The loss pushes up the policy’s log-likelihood of the chosen response and down the rejected response, while an implicit KL-like term against a frozen reference model prevents collapse. It’s much simpler and more stable than PPO-based RLHF, at the cost of some sample efficiency on very large-scale runs.",
