    text: "[Practice packet 02 key · response · Q10] What’s the difference between a “process reward model” (PRM) and an “outcome reward model” (ORM)? An outcome reward model scores only the final answer -- right or wrong, end of story. A process reward model scores individual reasoning STEPS along the way, telling the policy which intermediate thoughts were helpful. PRMs give denser signal and can catch subtle errors mid-chain, but they need step-level labels and can be over-optimized. ORMs are simpler but give sparser feedback. Evaluation (Arena and LLM-as-Judge)",
