    text: "[Practice packet 02 key · measure · Q3] LLM quantization (e.g., INT8 or INT4) reduces model size and speeds up inference. What is the core tradeoff? Quantization replaces the high-precision floats (FP16/BF16) in the model’s weights with lower-precision integer representations. The tradeoff is model quality -- aggressive quantization (e.g., 3-bit) can start to degrade output quality, while modest quantization (INT8, INT4 with good scaling) is nearly lossless for many tasks. You’re trading a small accuracy hit for large memory savings and throughput gains.",
