    sourceLabel: "Practice packet 02 key",
    text: "[Practice packet 02 key · Efficient Inference · Q5] FlashAttention changed how attention is computed at scale. What problem does it solve and, at a high level, how? Standard attention materializes an N×N attention matrix in GPU HBM, which for long sequences is both memory-expensive (O(N²) memory) and slow due to HBM reads/writes. FlashAttention is IO-aware: it computes attention in tiles that fit in the GPU’s fast SRAM and never materializes the full matrix, recomputing what it needs instead of writing and reading intermediate results. Net effect: faster attention and dramatically lower memory use, enabling much longer context lengths.",
