    text: "[Practice packet 02 key · scratch? · Q6] What is Constitutional AI (RLAIF), and how does it differ from standard RLHF? Constitutional AI uses the LLM itself (or another LLM) to generate the preference data, guided by a written set of principles (“a constitution”) -- e.g., the AI critiques its own outputs against the constitution and picks preferred responses. Standard RLHF requires human annotators to produce preference pairs; Constitutional AI replaces or augments them with AI-generated preferences, which is much cheaper and more scalable. The tradeoff is that the AI’s judgments inherit the constitution’s framing and any of the AI’s own biases.",
